Garden
[trigger none]
[vignette dungeons/the_hermitage]

The man seems small in the dirt. Puttering at work any of the younger brothers could do in a minute. Something to fill the hours while the rest carry the weight of the place.

choices:

* "Who are you?" [requires !tag hermitage.aldous_whoami]
    The old man smiles, and gazes at you with sightless eyes.

    "Just an old bag of sticks, here to keep the starlings away. Once a soldier, but you didn't ask that. But you must mean my name. I am called Aldous. Who are you stranger, and I don't mean your name."

    You explain you are a guild trader, a wanderer walking a nearby road.

    "And you still wear those fine rings?"

    You assure him you do.
    +add_tag hermitage.aldous_whoami
    +open Garden

* "Osric says you fought together" [requires !tag hermitage.aldous_fought && tag hermitage.aldous_whoami]
    "Osric says a lot of things. I think, even after all this time, he's still a little proud of what we did back then. Tell me, guild trader, have you served? Have you seen war?"

    You have not.

    "And yet you carry a weapon, even here in the garden. Perhaps you mean to cut the high grass on the hill?"

    You explain you were never asked to disarm.

    "Of course. I forget the new rules."
    +add_tag hermitage.aldous_fought
    +open Garden

* "What do you make of the deserters?" [requires !tag hermitage.aldous_deserters]
    +add_tag hermitage.aldous_deserters
    +open Aldus

* Return to the tower
    You walk back to the tower, uncertain whether you've gotten any answers.
    +open Tower